+## XVIII.7 The LLVM backend
+
+Restored from 0.9.8 by ODR-087.
+
+* `[CG-LL-1]` *(new in 0.9.9)* **Two backends over one intermediate representation.** The reference
+  implementation has two backends over the same MIR: C11 (§XVIII.1), for bootstrap and portability,
+  and LLVM, for optimisation control. The C backend comes first. The LLVM backend is begun once the C
+  backend passes the full conformance suite, and becomes the default once it also passes the
+  performance suite; until it exists, `--backend llvm` and `backend = "llvm"` are refused as not yet
+  implemented. The C backend stays supported afterwards: it is how Ember reaches every platform that
+  has a C compiler.
+* `[CG-LL-2]` *(new in 0.9.9)* The LLVM backend maps MIR to LLVM IR with the C backend's type mapping
+  and meets every requirement of this Part that is not about C specifically: no undefined behaviour
+  in its output, checked arithmetic through LLVM's overflow intrinsics, and the floating-point rules
+  of `[TYP-9]` and `[DET-5]`. It implements the platform C ABI's classification of arguments and
+  results itself (`[FFI-9]`), and lowers `std.simd`'s vector types to LLVM's (`[SIMD-1]`).
+* `[CG-LL-3]` *(new in 0.9.9)* It passes the borrow checker's facts to LLVM as `noalias`, `readonly`,
+  `dereferenceable(N)` and `nonnull` attributes, under the rule that governs the C backend's
+  `restrict` (`[SIMD-3]`: derived, never assumed); emits DWARF or CodeView debug information with
+  Ember's type names; and supports profile-guided optimisation through LLVM's instrumentation and
+  ThinLTO (`[BLD-6]`).
